Make DBusMenu GetLayout children spec-conformant (av of variants).

The DBusMenu protocol declares menu children as `av` (array of
variants), and the GetLayout out_signature on this very class already
says `u(ia{sv}av)`. The current code, however, builds the children
container with `dbus.Array(signature="(ia{sv}av)")`, which marshals
as `a(ia{sv}av)` (array of structs) on the wire. dbus-python does
not auto-rewrap, so non-conformant clients (e.g. HyprPanel's
astal-tray, which uses the strict `(i@a{sv}@av)` GVariant format)
crash with:

    GLib-CRITICAL: the GVariant format string '(i@a{sv}@av)' has a
    type of '(ia{sv}av)' but the given value has a type of
    '(ia{sv}a(ia{sv}av))'

Fix by changing the children array signature to `v` and tagging each
child Struct with `variant_level=1` so dbus-python emits the
spec-conformant `av` shape. Hosts that previously accepted the
struct-array form still accept the variant form (it's the documented
shape).

diff --git a/proton/vpn/app/gtk/widgets/main/tray_icon.py b/proton/vpn/app/gtk/widgets/main/tray_icon.py
index caeb91b..f00f00f 100644
--- a/proton/vpn/app/gtk/widgets/main/tray_icon.py
+++ b/proton/vpn/app/gtk/widgets/main/tray_icon.py
@@ -151,12 +151,12 @@ class _DBusMenuService(dbus.service.Object):
             return (
                 dbus.Int32(parent_id),
                 dbus.Dictionary({}, signature="sv"),
-                dbus.Array([], signature="(ia{sv}av)")
+                dbus.Array([], signature="v")
             )

         item: dbus.Dictionary = menu[parent_id]

-        children = dbus.Array([], signature="(ia{sv}av)")
+        children = dbus.Array([], signature="v")
         if "children" in item:
             for child_id in item["children"]:
                 child_layout = self._build_layout(child_id, properties, menu)
@@ -164,11 +164,12 @@ class _DBusMenuService(dbus.service.Object):
                 child_props = child_layout[1] \
                     if child_layout[1] else dbus.Dictionary({}, signature="sv")
                 child_children = child_layout[2] \
-                    if child_layout[2] else dbus.Array([], signature="(ia{sv}av)")
+                    if child_layout[2] else dbus.Array([], signature="v")
                 children.append(
                     dbus.Struct(
                         (child_id_dbus, child_props, child_children),
-                        signature="(ia{sv}av)"
+                        signature="(ia{sv}av)",
+                        variant_level=1
                     )
                 )

